The next result is due to Gubeladze, cf. \cite[Corrolary 7.4]{gubeladze1992elementary}.

\begin{lemma}{\rm (Local-global principle)}\label{lg}
	Let $A = A_0 \oplus A_1\oplus A_2 \oplus \cdots~$  be a graded ring and $n\geq3$. Let $\v \in \Um_{n}(A)$ such that the natural image of $\v$ in $\Um_n(A_0)$ is $e_1$. If $\v_{\m} \sim_{\E_n(A_{\m})} (e_1)_{\m}$ for all $\m \in \max(A_0)$, then $\v \sim_{\E_n(A)} e_1$.
\end{lemma}


