\end{figure}

\paragraph{Pulsar-timing arrays (PTAs).}
Second-order scalar perturbations and early PBH binaries generate a
stochastic gravitational-wave background (GWB) peaked at
$f_{\rm PTA}\!\sim\!{\cal O}(\mathrm{nHz})$.
Our fiducial spectrum predicts
\(\Omega_{\rm GW}h^{2}\!\simeq\!10^{-10}\) at $f=4\,\mathrm{nHz}$,
marginally below the NANOGrav 15-yr common-spectrum detection
\cite{NANOGrav2023}.  The full signal space accessible to PTAs is
visualized in Figure~\ref{fig:GWB_PTA}.

