\begin{enumerate}[1.]
    \item {\bf Novel family of linear programs}. We introduce a novel family of linear programs $\plpm$, each associated with a set of possible matches $\m{M} \subseteq \m{T} \times \m{T}$. We show that certain ``suitable'' solutions of $\plpm$ map naturally to greedy policies.
