{\bf Dynamic Matching with Abandonment.} \citet{collina2020dynamic} and \citet{aouad2022dynamic} study the same model as we do.  \citet{collina2020dynamic} finds a policy that guarantees $1/8$ of the omniscient policy, while  \citet{aouad2022dynamic}  offer a guarantee of $\frac{1}{4}(1-1/e) \approx .158$ against the optimal {\em online} policy. \citet{li2023fully} study a discrete version of this model with general (non-exponential) sojourn times and under mild conditions on this sojourn time, find an online policy that achieves a competitive ratio of $0.155$. 


