For any time $t\ge 0$, construct a weighted graph $G(t) = (\mathcal{A}(t), \mathcal{E}(t), w_t)$ where each vertex $a \in \mathcal{A}(t)$ represents an agent who arrived before time $t$, agents are connected by an edge if they were present at the pool at the same time, and the weight of each edge is the reward that would be obtained by matching these agents: %\na{should this be $w(t)$? seems like it depends on $t$} with
