\begin{definition}
    Let $\m{H}(t) = \{(i_a, t_a,d_a)\}_{a \in \mathcal{A}(t)}$ be the history up to time $t$. A policy $\pi$ maps the history $\m{H}(t)$ to a matching of $G(t)$. We use $\pi(\m{H}(t))$ to denote the matching chosen by policy $\pi$ at time $t$. %\na{Do we have notation for these sets?}
\end{definition}
