It is worth noting that we do not impose any informational constraints to $\pi$, nor do we require it to be ``consistent'' across time. For example, if only two agents arrive before time $t$, then when we optimize for time $t$, $\pi$ might match these two agents. When we optimize for a longer horizon, $\pi$ may choose to make a different match with these agents. 

