We use $V(\pi, \m{I}, t)$ to be the expected reward rate of policy $\pi$ in instance $\m{I}$ by time $t\ge 0$.
\[V(\pi, \m{I}, t) = \frac{1}{t} \E{\sum_{(a,b) \in \pi(\m{H}(t))}w_t(a,b)} \]
