Here the expectation is taken over the random arrival and departure process (that is, the sets $\mathcal{A}_i(t)$ and times $\{t_a,d_a\}_{a \in \mathcal{A}(t)}$, which induce the graph $G(t)$).
For any time $t>0$ and any graph $G(t)$, the omniscient policy always returns a maximum weight matching of $G(t)$.
