\section{Results}

\label{sec:results}
The previous sections described the methods used to identify greedy policies. We succintly describe the entire procedure in the following definition.
\begin{definition}
    For an instance $\m{I}$, $\alg$ is the greedy policy corresponding to the optimal suitable solution of $\plpm$, where $\m{M}$ is the result of running \Cref{algo:suitability}.
\end{definition}
In this section we present the intermediate results that jointly imply \Cref{thm:emu:result}: $\alg$ achieves at least half of the omniscient benchmark if departures are homogeneous.

