    \end{align}
    This is true for any sets $S, S' \subseteq \mathcal{T}$ type $i \in \mathcal{T}$ and so we can bound the rate of matches using $E[W(t)]/t$ which matches the constraints described in \eqref{eq:offlinematchrate2}. It is easy to see that $\frac{1}{t} \E{X_{ij}^\pi}(t) \ge 0$ since this is a counting process and therefore \eqref{eq:posrate2} follows.
