\begin{proof}
    Fix a Markovian policy $\pi$ and let $N^\pi$ be a random variable drawn from the steady-state distribution of $N^{\pi}(t)$. Fix a set $S$ such that $\mu_i = \mu$ for all $i \in S$ and let $\lambda = \sum_{i\in S} \lambda_i$.  Let $q_k$ be the steady-state probability there are $k$ agents of type $i \in S$ in the system:
    \begin{equation}
        q_k = \mathbb{P}(\sum_{i \in S} N^\pi_i = k) \quad \forall k \in \mathbb{N}_0
    \end{equation}
    From \Cref{lemma:boundq:generalpolicies} we know that for any Markovian policy:
