\begin{abstract}                % Abstract of 50--100 words
The integration of Industry 4.0 technologies into engineering workflows is an essential step toward automating and optimizing plant and process engineering processes. The \ac{AAS} serves as a key enabler for creating interoperable Digital Twins that facilitate engineering data exchange and automation. This paper explores the use of AAS within engineering workflows, particularly in combination with \ac{BPMN} to define structured and automated processes. We propose a distributed AAS copy-on-write infrastructure that enhances security and scalability while enabling seamless cross organizational collaboration. We also introduce a workflow management prototype automating AAS operations and engineering workflows, improving efficiency and traceability. 
%The paper concludes with an outlook on the future of standardized workflows in industrial automation.
Our results indicate a great potential of BPMN on both AAS infrastructure and business process sides.
\end{abstract}

\begin{keyword}
Process and Plant Engineering Workflow, Automation, Industry 4.0, Digital Twin, Asset Administration Shell, AAS, Business Process Model and Notation, BPMN 
\end{keyword}

