We construct this interaction potential as an array in momentum space, before performing successive SVDs to put into MPS form. The resultant bond dimension scalings for various truncations and interaction Radii $\mathbf{R}$ are illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:app_trunc_Udd}. We observe that the resultant bond dimensions are larger for smaller truncation radii, and still grow with system size. It can be seen that as $R\rightarrow \infty$, we recover the same scaling as the fully periodic treatment in Fig.~\ref{fig:dipole_dims}.




